<!--
  The container in its working state with one finished bay passing out
  through an open side, for tests/container_test.cc and for looking at.

    bazel run //:viewer_container

  The container stands at the world's origin. The bay's tube lies along the
  container at the height bay.xml gives it, exactly in the plane of the
  container's -X side: half of every module is still inside and half is
  out. That is how a bay leaves, since a module is 2.382 m long and the
  container 2.330 m wide inside. Between the corner posts the bay has
  0.035 m to spare at each end.

  Where the bay stands here says nothing about a layout: no conveyor, no
  support and no arm is drawn, and the bay hangs where its file puts it.
-->
<mujoco model="container scene">
  <include file="common.xml"/>
  <include file="container.xml"/>
  <include file="bay.xml"/>
</mujoco>
